WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
Start with a real flow.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:07.324
In Q Agent Extension, press Record, update the release name, and save the draft.

3
00:00:07.324 --> 00:00:11.479
Stop recording, then add the expected result: Draft saved.

4
00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:14.577
Review the captured steps before replaying.

5
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:17.093
Replay on a reset page.

6
00:00:17.093 --> 00:00:23.089
Q Agent returns to the starting address, enters the recorded value, and clicks Save draft.

7
00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.790
The assertion checks the actual outcome.

8
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.755
Save the passing test to your local library.

9
00:00:29.766 --> 00:00:32.075
Choose a framework and copy the script.

10
00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:38.055
This is the actual Playwright export, with navigation, recorded selectors, and the expected outcome.

11
00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:40.778
We also run this copied script independently.

12
00:00:40.778 --> 00:00:44.923
Review generated code before using it in your own automation project.

13
00:00:45.939 --> 00:00:47.640
A passing click is not enough.

14
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.798
Here we deliberately expect an approval message that the sample application does not show.

15
00:00:52.798 --> 00:00:53.705
The test fails.

16
00:00:53.705 --> 00:00:59.431
Review the assertion and the evidence in the side panel before changing the test or the application.

17
00:01:00.442 --> 00:01:02.032
Run saved tests together.

18
00:01:02.032 --> 00:01:06.865
This local example replays the recorded draft flow and checks a sample API.

19
00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:10.808
Review the outcome of each case and the overall quality gate.

20
00:01:10.808 --> 00:01:14.369
These are real execution results, not a mock interface.
